# Multi-omics uncover interactions in the vaginal microbiome and a type II secretion/Tad pilus system in *Gardnerella* species

🌐 **Browse the interactive site:** https://fabriciorgki.github.io/Gardnerella-multiomics/

This site hosts the interactive syntenic maps of the *Gardnerella* pangenome,
together with the R scripts used to reproduce the analyses in this study.

## About

Long-read sequencing of clinical *Gardnerella* isolates revealed a pangenomic
split between *G. vaginalis* and *G. piotii* that correlates with high- versus
low-biofilm phenotypes, linked to clade-specific genomic islands and allelic
variants. Integrating pangenome, proteome, 16S, and metabolome data across
pairwise co-cultures of five key vaginal bacteria showed that *G. vaginalis* and
*L. iners* act as dominant ecological drivers, and implicated a putative
type II secretion/Tad pilus operon in interspecies interactions — an operon more
abundant in BV samples than in healthy controls. Metabolomics further identified
methyl-β-carboline and dipeptides that shape growth and biofilm formation of
vaginal microbes (and inhibit multidrug-resistant pathogens), suggesting new
strategies for managing polymicrobial infections.

## Site structure

| Folder | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `Syntenic_Pangenome/` | Interactive syntenic map of the pangenome |
| `Gene_maps/` | R scripts for gene mapping |
| `Proteomics/` | R scripts for proteomic analyses |
| `Putative-Operons/` | R scripts for putative operon analyses |
| `Putative-Operons/pangenome_operons/` | Interactive pangenome operon viewer |
| `Metabolomics/` | R scripts for metabolomic analyses |
| `Growth_&_biofilm_assays/` | R scripts for growth and biofilm assays |

Each script folder contains its own documentation describing inputs, outputs,
and required R packages. Set the working directory and adjust file paths, group
labels, and condition palettes at the top of each script before running.
